{"study_accession":"PRJNA961116","secondary_study_accession":"SRP434182","title":"Sphingosine-1 phosphate receptor 1 (S1PR1) is crucial for maintaining the stem cell properties of acute myeloid leukemia stem cells","description":"To identify the most important gene(s) for maintaining the stem cell properties of leukemia stem cells (LSCs), we analyzed the transcriptional profiles of LSC and non-LSC subsets from acute leukemia patients and identified S1PR1 as a novel biomarker of LSCs. Then to understand the underlying mechanisms of S1PR1-dependent stemness maintenance, we performed gene expression profiling analyses comparing CD34+S1PR1+ and CD34+S1PR1- cell fractions from AML patients and healthy donors; we also determined the global transcriptional response of KG1 cells to an inhibitor of S1PR1 (FTY720) at two concentrations. Overall design: Data set 1: Three acute myeloid leukemia (AML) samples (patient #M1, #M2, and #M3) were sorted into paired LSC (CD34+CD38-) and non-LSC (CD34+CD38+, CD34-CD38+, and CD34-CD38-) fractions by flow cytometry. RNA-seq profiling was performed on the paired fractions for each individual. Data set 2: Three Philadelphia chromosome-positive B cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) samples (patient #L1, #L2, and #L3) were sorted into paired LSC (CD34+CD38-CD58-) and non-LSC (CD34+CD38+CD58+, CD34+CD38+CD58-, and CD34+CD38-CD58+) fractions by flow cytometry. RNA-seq profiling was performed on the paired fractions for each individual. Data set 3: RNA-seq profiling was performed on CD34+S1PR1+ (labeled as P_pos) and CD34+S1PR1- (labeled as P_neg) bone marrow mononuclear cell fractions from AML patients (patient #9 and #10) purified by flow cytometry. Data set 4: RNA-seq profiling was performed on CD34+S1PR1+ (labeled as D_pos) and CD34+S1PR1- (labeled as D_neg) bone marrow mononuclear cell fractions from healthy donors (donor #1 and #2) purified by flow cytometry. Data set 5: RNA-seq profiling was performed on KG1 cells that were pre-treated with FTY720 at 3 μM (labeled as F3) or 4 μM (labeled as F4) for 24 h or sham treatment (labeled as F0) without FTY720.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":54,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN34353306","study_accession":"PRJNA961116","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"D2_neg_B(rep2)","description":"D2_neg_B(rep2)","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7221908","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-08-25","attributes":[["source_name","Bone marrow"],["tissue","Bone marrow"],["cell_type","CD34+S1PR1- bone marrow mononuclear cells"],["genotype","WT"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR24288343","experiment_accession":"SRX20083892","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":44633258,"base_count":13389977400,"first_public":"2024-08-25","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7221908: D2_neg_B(rep2) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN34353307","study_accession":"PRJNA961116","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"D2_neg_A(rep1)","description":"D2_neg_A(rep1)","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7221907","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-08-25","attributes":[["source_name","Bone marrow"],["tissue","Bone marrow"],["cell_type","CD34+S1PR1- bone marrow mononuclear cells"],["genotype","WT"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR24288344","experiment_accession":"SRX20083891","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":48154032,"base_count":14446209600,"first_public":"2024-08-25","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7221907: D2_neg_A(rep1) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN34353308","study_accession":"PRJNA961116","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"D2_pos_B(rep2)","description":"D2_pos_B(rep2)","sex":"","geo_sample":